sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-sugimura-tracheal-viscous-fingering> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-sugimura-tracheal-viscous-fingering-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-sugimura-tracheal-viscous-fingering-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Nelson et al. (2017) Development & Kim et al. (2015) Dev. Cell microfluidic transmural pressure, Laplace epithelial wall stress, ASM peristalsis, 3D ellipsoidal pleural cavity tree, Poiseuille/CFTR luminal pressure network and laryngeal valve cycles driving embryonic lung branching — MorphoEval overall 90.9/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 3 (v3) evaluation of `2015-sugimura-tracheal-viscous-fingering.py` (overall weighted score: 90.9/100, down from 94.0/100 in v2). The single v2 remediation item is closed as an honest reduced model: a 3D orthogonal-bifurcation tree inside an analytic ellipsoidal pleural cavity with pleura-contact arrest and a cavity-scale ablation; spatially resolved CFTR/NKCC1 chloride secretion feeding a Hagen-Poiseuille luminal pressure network (intra-tree drop 6.0e-6 of Delta P, so the 2D uniform-pressure assumption is validated, not refuted); and laryngeal valve opening/closing cycles with an exact-exponential ODE, an 11-point duty sweep (Spearman rho = -1.0; occlusion/open fold ratio 6.844 vs Nelson-derived 6.728) and the Jensen gap of the Hill rate. Two new Lean 4 laws (5 total, 0 sorrys), 7 new measurements (16 total), 4 new self-test suites (12 total, 0.9 s), 3x3 figure, 3D figure, GIF 3D pane and two new CLI flags. The score falls because this round surfaced defects the v2 audit did not penalise: specimen measurements 7-9 compare the segmentation against its own recorded outputs (reference == value by construction), the 8-point `*_obs` columns are fitted targets rather than digitised figures, the file name / seed paper / organism (Gallus gallus, Nelson 2015, viscous fingering) do not describe what the script models (Mus musculus; Nelson 2017 / Kim 2015 / Unbekandt 2008; Hill-rate exponential branching), the 3D tip count is inherited from the 0-D Hill solver, the valve model is fetal-sheep in-utero physiology applied to a larynx-free explant claim, the four new DOIs are unverified offline, and a stale comment cites a non-existent `calibrate_laryngeal_resistance` function. Overall 90.9/100 (faithfulness 90.4, reproducibility 91.9); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 171769b9; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 91, Morphological realism / specimen match 90, Parameter expressivity 94, Morphometric validation 88, Source and data traceability 89, Code-to-model traceability 91, Reproducibility package 95. Output judged: docs/media/tracheal_viscous_fingering_comparison.png: rendered output of 2015-sugimura-tracheal-viscous-fingering.py at 171769b9, image/png, 1181381 B, 2488×2390 px, artifact_sha256 09f315b864825744e84dc0ae0fc370db9e8f4edc97d3b21187a9c509586d9730 (sha256 09f315b864825744e84dc0ae0fc370db9e8f4edc97d3b21187a9c509586d9730), spec_fingerprint b14c2a9f28075322a3f6f059ad4e5c0d7c9dc62fb5a6e7b4d98bf273506f3edc. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: b14c2a9f28075322a3f6f059ad4e5c0d7c9dc62fb5a6e7b4d98bf273506f3edc; artifact_sha256: 09f315b864825744e84dc0ae0fc370db9e8f4edc97d3b21187a9c509586d9730; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/tracheal_viscous_fingering/embryonic_lung_branching_specimen.jpg=8086ebb8b44cbdff..., datasets/tracheal_viscous_fingering/paper_citations.bib=f89245946bd44e2a..., datasets/tracheal_viscous_fingering/pleural_cavity_valve_reference.json=6a77bbd2b7744570..., datasets/tracheal_viscous_fingering/scout_manifest.json=5ca9d0b7e3b9f2d2..., datasets/tracheal_viscous_fingering/tracheal_viscous_fingering_reference.json=da4d1143ccb80d60...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-tracheal-viscous-fingering-audit-v2. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Nelson, Gleghorn, Myers, Radisky & Stone (2017) Development 144:4328-4335 microfluidic chest cavity experiments proving that embryonic lung branching rate dN_tips/dt and synchronized airway smooth muscle (ASM) peristaltic wave frequency f_ASM depend strictly on the transmural pressure difference Delta P = P_lumen - P_pleura and are invariant under common-mode hydrostatic pressure shifts (P_lumen + P_0, P_pleura + P_0) | Laplace-Young circumferential epithelial wall stress sigma_theta = Delta P * R / h driving mechanosensitive FGF10/ERK1/2/Etv4 distal tip proliferation and bifurcation above critical threshold Delta P_c approx 50 Pa (Unbekandt et al. 2008 Mech. Dev. 125:314-324; Nelson et al. 2017) | Kim et al. (2015) Dev. Cell 34:668-681 & Nelson et al. (2017) nifedipine L-type Ca2+ channel blockade of ASM peristaltic contractions or tracheal intubation drainage (Delta P <= 0 Pa) collapsing terminal bud bifurcation | Olver & Strang (1974) chloride-driven fetal lung-liquid secretion with distal > proximal secretory activity; Harding et al. (1986) and Harding & Hooper (1996) fetal-sheep upper-airway resistance dominating lung-liquid efflux, a closed-glottis tracheal pressure plateau of 1-2 mmHg, and a laryngeal resistance drop during fetal breathing-movement episodes; Metzger et al. (2008) orthogonal bifurcation mode of the mouse bronchial tree; reconstructed_in_script: Coupled 2D spatial microfluidic bronchial tree and Laplace wall stress solver (`simulate_2d_microfluidic_lung_tree`) plus 8-point Delta P in [0, 400] Pa sweep (`evaluate_transmural_pressure_sweep`), reproducing the vendored 48h terminal bud counts (Pearson r = 0.99997), branching rate Gamma_branch and ASM contraction frequency f_ASM columns | Exact common-mode gauge invariance verification across (P_lumen, P_pleura) = (200, 0), (0, -200), and (500, 300) Pa (max deviation = 0.0000) for the 2D, 3D and valve solvers, alongside nifedipine Ca2+ channel blockade and tracheal drainage negative controls | (Pass 3) 3D bifurcating tree grown inside an analytic ellipsoidal pleural cavity with 90-degree rotating bifurcation planes and pleura-contact tip arrest (`simulate_3d_pleural_cavity_lung_tree`), with a cavity-scale ablation 0.7-2.0 at 300 Pa (`evaluate_pleural_cavity_ablation`: contact fractions 0.50/0.50/0.25/0.00/0.00) | (Pass 3) Spatially resolved CFTR/NKCC1 chloride secretion j_Cl(g) (geometric proximal-to-distal gradient, 6x) integrated over segment epithelial area and a Hagen-Poiseuille resistor-network luminal pressure solve P_node = P_amn + R_larynx Q_tot + sum_path R_i Q_i (`solve_tree_luminal_pressure`); intra-tree drop 6.0e-6 of the 200 Pa tracheal Delta P | (Pass 3) Laryngeal valve opening/closing cycles C dP/dt = Q - (P - P_amn)/R_larynx(t) integrated exactly per step over 48 h with an 11-point open-duty sweep (Spearman rho = -1.0, occlusion/open fold ratio 6.844 vs 6.728 reference) and the Jensen gap of the Hill branching rate (-0.0226 day^-1 at duty 0.40) (`simulate_laryngeal_valve_cycles`, `evaluate_laryngeal_duty_cycle_sweep`) | Computer-vision segmentation (`segment_embryonic_lung_specimen`) of the vendored Mus musculus pseudoglandular E11-E16.5 embryonic lung specimen (`embryonic_lung_branching_specimen.jpg`, CC BY 3.0) extracting 17 distal terminal buds, distal-to-total airway area fraction = 0.6885, and mean distal tip radius = 3.8470 +- 1.3152 px; transfer_boundary: 2D projected bronchial tree and continuum Laplace hoop stress field mapped to whole-mount E11.5-E16.5 pseudoglandular mouse lung explants in microfluidic chest chambers | The pleural cavity is an analytic ellipsoid (CAVITY_SEMI_AXES, CHEST_LENGTH_SCALE_UM = 1.6 mm) and not a stereolithographic STL chest mesh; no lobation or left-right asymmetry; generation depth of the 3D tree is inherited from the same 0-D Hill N(t) as the 2D solver, so the 3D tip count is a consistency check and not an emergent prediction | The laryngeal valve / fetal-breathing-movement model transfers fetal-sheep in-utero physiology (Harding 1986/1996) to the explant setting of Nelson et al. (2017), whose cannulated explants have no larynx; the closed-glottis plateau (250 Pa), R_open/R_closed (0.25), duty (0.40), period (40 min) and tau_closed (6 min) are model choices flagged `provenance: model` in `pleural_cavity_valve_reference.json` | CFTR secretion is a prescribed functional form (geometric gradient), not a transcript-map-derived field; the laryngeal resistance in the 3D solver is back-solved so that the tracheal inlet pressure equals p_lumen_pa, so the tracheal Delta P is a boundary condition and only the intra-tree distribution is emergent | The `*_obs` sweep columns of `tracheal_viscous_fingering_reference.json` are not literal digitisations of Nelson 2017 figures (no figure/table coordinates or digitisation provenance) and the Hill constants were fitted to them, so the Pearson r ~ 0.9999 correlations are largely self-referential; does_not_claim: Saffman-Taylor viscous fingering or any Hele-Shaw interfacial instability (despite the file name and campaign slug, no viscous-fingering mathematics exists in the script); Gallus gallus data (the vendored specimen and all vendored references are Mus musculus and fetal sheep) | Full 3D Navier-Stokes Stokesian fluid-structure interaction of individual ciliated epithelial cells, single-channel CaV1.2 gating kinetics, lobar branching programme sequences, or in-utero FBM pressure traces measured in the mouse." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: 2015-sugimura-tracheal-viscous-fingering.py:1-11, morphoeval/cloud/dispatches/slot-059.json — the file name / slug (\"sugimura\", \"viscous fingering\"), the dispatch organism (Gallus gallus) and the campaign seed paper (Nelson 2015, 10.1242/dev.119123) do not describe the script (Mus musculus; Nelson 2017 / Kim 2015 / Unbekandt 2008; no Saffman-Taylor mathematics). Either add a genuine Hele-Shaw / Saffman-Taylor luminal fingering sub-model with a chick (Gallus gallus) specimen, or record the identity correction in the dispatch, README and math-KG so the claim boundary and the campaign metadata agree.",
            "remediation needed: 2015-sugimura-tracheal-viscous-fingering.py:1219 and 1335-1342 — replace the hard-coded \"(4.71x)\" literal and the 1.18 / 1.00 `obs_vals_e` entries with values formatted from `controls` and read from `perturbation_controls` in the reference JSON; fix the Panel E legend overlap and give Panels G / GIF 3D pane an ellipsoid wireframe and lobe shading so the cavity is legible.",
            "remediation needed: 2015-sugimura-tracheal-viscous-fingering.py:389-391 and 480-621 — the pleural cavity is an analytic ellipsoid (`CAVITY_SEMI_AXES`, `CAVITY_CENTER`) with no lobation or left-right asymmetry. Replace it with a lobated chest / pleural mesh (vendored STL or segmented microCT of an E12.5-E14.5 mouse thorax, SHA-256 pinned, with provenance) and grow left (1 lobe) / right (4 lobes) trees so that pleura-contact arrest is compared against a real geometry rather than against the solver's own unconfined ablation.",
            "remediation needed: 2015-sugimura-tracheal-viscous-fingering.py:393-394 and 412-417 — `J_CL_PROX/DIST` magnitudes and the geometric 6x gradient are order-of-magnitude model choices. Derive the CFTR/NKCC1 secretion field from a published proximal-distal expression map (digitised, with figure coordinates) and sweep the gradient ratio so that the \"intra-tree drop is negligible\" conclusion (measurement 14) is tested rather than assumed.",
            "remediation needed: 2015-sugimura-tracheal-viscous-fingering.py:495-499 and 600 — the 3D generation depth is inherited from the 0-D `simulate_buds_48h` and the per-tip Gamma(Delta P_tip) at L600 never feeds back into growth, so measurement 15 (3D tips = 2D tips) is a consistency check. Make tip-level branching emergent: advance each tip with its own Gamma(Delta P_tip) and let pleural contact / secretion gradient alter the tip count.",
            "remediation needed: 2015-sugimura-tracheal-viscous-fingering.py:573-580 — the comment cites a non-existent `calibrate_laryngeal_resistance` and `R_larynx` is back-solved so the tracheal inlet equals `p_lumen_pa`. Either implement the calibration (R_larynx fixed from the closed-glottis plateau and let Delta P_trachea emerge from Q_total / R_larynx) or correct the comment and state the boundary-condition nature in the docstring and math-KG.",
            "remediation needed: 2015-sugimura-tracheal-viscous-fingering.py:635-691 and 1763 — the FBM valve model transfers fetal-sheep in-utero physiology to a larynx-free explant claim, its time-averaged Delta P (154.3 Pa) misses the 200 Pa reference by 23 %, and the self-test accepts 100-280 Pa. Source a mouse / in-utero pressure trace or explicitly reclassify the measurement as a transfer prediction, tighten the tolerance, and expose the valve constants (`R_OPEN_OVER_R_CLOSED`, `FBM_PERIOD_MIN_DEFAULT`, `TAU_CLOSED_MIN`) to the CLI / a sweep.",
            "remediation needed: datasets/tracheal_viscous_fingering/paper_citations.bib:47-92 and 2015-sugimura-tracheal-viscous-fingering.py:381 — verify the four new DOIs (olver1974, harding1986, harding1996, metzger2008) online and clear the `doi_verified_offline: false` flags; add a bib entry for McCray et al. 1992 or remove the comment citation.",
            "remediation needed: datasets/tracheal_viscous_fingering/tracheal_viscous_fingering_reference.json and 2015-sugimura-tracheal-viscous-fingering.py:98-108 — the 8-point `*_obs` sweep columns have no figure/table digitisation provenance and the Hill constants were fitted to them, so measurements 1-3 (r ~ 0.9999) are self-referential. Digitise Nelson 2017 Figs. 1-3 (and Unbekandt 2008 occlusion data) with coordinates and error bars, record the digitisation in the JSON, and refit / report held-out error.",
            "remediation needed: datasets/tracheal_viscous_fingering/tracheal_viscous_fingering_reference.json:46-55 and 2015-sugimura-tracheal-viscous-fingering.py:1082-1111, 1718-1722 — `empirical_morphometrics` (17 buds, 0.6885, 3.8470 px) are the script's own outputs, so specimen measurements 7-9 and self-test suite 7 compare the segmentation against itself. Replace with an independent manual count / annotation of the specimen (or a published bud count for the stage) with provenance, and drop the `*_pred` columns from the reference file.",
            "remediation needed: morphoeval/math_kg_loops/sugimura-tracheal-viscous-fingering.yaml:50, 72, 95 — the `code_locus` ranges for laws 1-3 (L120-L195, L140-L215, L150-L320) are stale against the current 1834-line script (equations at L153-225, 2D solver at L232-362); re-pin them, and strengthen the Lean module beyond Int-linear statements (e.g. prove the Jensen inequality direction for the convex-below-K_P Hill rate or the exact-exponential update's monotonicity) so the theorems speak to the ODE and the nonlinearity actually simulated." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.909"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Gemini 4 Argon (MorphoEval Autonomous Loop Slot 059 Pass 3 Assessor)" ;
        dct:identifier "gemini-4-argon" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> ;
        foaf:homepage <https://deepmind.google> .
}

